  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has rough, reddish-brown bark that peels away in thin strips, providing a tactile experience for students. The glossy, evergreen leaves can be used in lessons on leaf structure and photosynthesis. It produces small, white to pink bell-shaped flowers that attract pollinators, offering a chance to study plant-pollinator interactions. The tree also bears round, red fruits that ripen in the fall, which can be used to explore topics like fruit development and seed dispersal.",
